	"story_jassim_ask": "My hens keep running off into the field. A small fence would save my mornings. Could you bring me 6 wood?",
	"story_jassim_row": "Give Jassim 6 wood for the fence",
	"story_jassim_done": "We built the fence together, post by post. The hens look offended, but they are staying home. I will share their eggs with you every week.",
	"story_jassim_eggs": "Jassim: \"Eggs from the fenced hens, %d for you.\"",
	"story_jassim_thanks": "Your grandfather once fixed my roof without being asked. Now you fixed my fence. Kindness comes back around.",
	"story_elder_ask": "My eyes are tired, and small writing swims on the page. When you have found 3 of Saad's pages, would you read them to me?",
	"story_elder_row": "Read grandfather's pages to the elder",
	"story_elder_wait": "Come back when you have found %d of grandfather's pages.",
	"story_elder_done": "You read slowly, and he listens with his eyes closed. At the end he smiles: \"That is Saad's voice. Thank you for lending me your eyes.\"",
	"story_elder_thanks": "Since you read to me, I sit by the well each morning and tell the children Saad's stories. The village remembers him again.",
	"story_merchant_ask": "Everything on my stall comes from far away. I want to sell something from our own land. Bring me 5 of your best tomatoes?",
	"story_merchant_row": "Give the merchant 5 tomatoes",
	"story_merchant_done": "He sets your tomatoes at the front under a small sign: \"From the farm of Saad's grandson.\" They sell before noon.",
	"story_merchant_thanks": "People ask for your harvest by name now. A market should smell like its own soil.",
	"story_carpenter_ask": "I am teaching myself to carve small things, but my copper knife is worn out. Could you bring me 3 copper for a new one?",
